# DENY BY DEFAULT.
#
# This repo exists for one purpose: to give Kili a memory she can read on every
# scheduled run. It is NOT a backup of the Kiki folder.
#
# The Kiki folder holds real client PII (prospect names, emails, deal values, call
# transcripts) and large media. None of that belongs here. So everything is ignored
# and specific paths are added back below. A new file is invisible to git unless
# somebody deliberately allows it, which is the safe direction for a folder like
# this one to fail in.
#
# Before widening this list, ask whether Kili actually needs to read the file, and
# whether it names a client.

/*

!/.gitignore
!/README.md

# Her knowledge base. The whole point.
!/.claude/
/.claude/*
!/.claude/knowledge/

# Sandbox network allowlist, so a cloud run can reach slack.com and post as Kili
# rather than as Kiki. Confirmed 2026-08-22: the cloud sandbox routes egress through a
# policy-enforcing proxy and slack.com is not allowed by default, so her bot-token curl
# returned "CONNECT tunnel failed, response 403". Reading Slack works because that goes
# through the MCP connector. No secrets in this file, only two hostnames.
!/.claude/settings.json

# Her own definition and her specialists, so she knows her roster.
!/.claude/agents/

# Her entry point.
!/.claude/skills/
/.claude/skills/*
!/.claude/skills/kili/

# brd-agent is tracked and instructs loading these on every run, so without them a
# scheduled run of her BRD specialist has no house conventions at all. Recorded as a
# defect in knowledge/intake/handled.md on 2026-08-19 and fixed 2026-08-22.
# corpus-index.md is deliberately NOT admitted: its excluded-BRD section names eight
# clients, which is exactly what this repo exists to keep out.
!/.claude/skills/brd-writer/
/.claude/skills/brd-writer/*
!/.claude/skills/brd-writer/reference/
/.claude/skills/brd-writer/reference/*
!/.claude/skills/brd-writer/reference/conventions.md
!/.claude/skills/brd-writer/reference/page-types.md
!/.claude/skills/brd-writer/reference/house-template.md

# Charlie's weekly pipeline, so the cloud routine can read it. Carries no client
# data: it names the tracker by title pattern and reads it live at runtime.
!/.claude/skills/housing-content-calendar/

# Wrighter's build assets, so a scheduled run can draft while the Mac is off.
# A page template, a font stylesheet and the cover script. No client data in any
# of it, and the fonts are SIL Open Font Licence, which permits redistribution.
# The raw .woff2 sources stay out: fonts.css already embeds them base64, so
# shipping both is duplicate weight, and they are re-downloadable from Fontsource
# if a weight ever needs adding.
!/.claude/wrighter/
/.claude/wrighter/assets/fonts/

# Who she is, and the channel she currently reaches Kiki through.
!/kili/
/kili/*
!/kili/NOTICE.md
!/kili/channels/

# Belt and braces. These must never appear regardless of the rules above.
node_modules/
.venv/
.next/
*.mp4
*.mov
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.pdf
*.xlsx
*.csv
*.sqlite
*.db
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
